# Khovan Reach shared entity cleanup helpers.
#
# First file in scripts/lib/. Owns the reusable "remove a spawned contact"
# routine and the destroy-source attribution guard that goes with it.
#
# Why this is shared rather than copied per act, from
# docs/04_implementation_setup/95_scripts_lib_extraction_plan.md section 3.1:
# spawn/cleanup is the highest-reuse code in the remaining build. Slice 07B
# spawns Halcyon, Slice 10 spawns the cache, Slice 11 spawns two pirates, and
# Slice 12 destroys them. A defect here propagates to all four.
#
# OWNS NO STATE. Every flag this touches belongs to the caller and is passed in.
# A helper with its own `shared` state is a singleton, which breaks the moment
# two pirates need it at once - extraction plan section 4, rule 2.

# --- The destroy-hook hazard this exists to contain -------------------------
#
# Confirmed live 2026-08-09 (tests/SLICE06_VERIFICATION.md): sbs.delete_object()
# fires the same //damage/destroy hook a genuine Weapons kill fires, and it
# fires DEFERRED - the calling handler finishes first, and the destroy handler
# runs afterwards. Trace ordering across four independent cleanup events
# confirmed it.
#
# Two consequences that cost live sessions to learn:
#
#   1. A destroy handler cannot tell cleanup from a kill without a flag.
#   2. The flag must NOT be cleared by the caller after delete_object(), because
#      the destroy handler has not run yet. It is consumed (read and cleared) by
#      the destroy handler itself.
#
# So the contract here is: the caller sets its own *_cleanup_in_progress flag
# before calling, this helper deletes, and the caller's //damage/destroy handler
# reads-and-clears the flag. See khovan_entity_cleanup_note_deferred_destroy for
# the shape a caller's handler should use.

=== khovan_entity_cleanup_despawn_contact ===
    # Remove a spawned contact completely: navproxy, selections, then object.
    #
    # Params:
    #   cleanup_object_id   id of the spawned object, 0 if none
    #   cleanup_navproxy_id id of its navproxy, 0 if none
    #   cleanup_owner       caller name, for the trace only
    #
    # Order matters. The navproxy goes first because it references the object,
    # and selections are cleared before deletion so no console is left pointing
    # at an id that is about to stop existing.
    default cleanup_object_id = 0
    default cleanup_navproxy_id = 0
    default cleanup_owner = "unspecified"

    if cleanup_navproxy_id != 0:
        sim.delete_navproxy_by_id(cleanup_navproxy_id)

    if cleanup_object_id == 0:
        script.write_khovan_startup_trace(f"[KHOVAN LIB CLEANUP] owner={cleanup_owner} no object to remove")
        ->END

    # Clear all three selections. A console still selecting a deleted object is
    # the Slice 04 empty-Comms-panel failure class, and it is cheap to prevent.
    if artemis_id != 0:
        set_science_selection(artemis_id, 0)
        set_comms_selection(artemis_id, 0)
        set_weapons_selection(artemis_id, 0)

    sbs.delete_object(cleanup_object_id)
    script.write_khovan_startup_trace(f"[KHOVAN LIB CLEANUP] owner={cleanup_owner} object={cleanup_object_id} navproxy={cleanup_navproxy_id} removed")
    ->END

=== khovan_entity_cleanup_note_deferred_destroy ===
    # Documentation label. Callers do not schedule this; it exists so the
    # required destroy-handler shape lives next to the cleanup routine rather
    # than only in a verification record.
    #
    # A caller's //damage/destroy handler must look like this:
    #
    #     //damage/destroy if has_role(DESTROYED_ID, "<your_role>")
    #         if <your>_cleanup_in_progress:
    #             <your>_destruction_source = "cleanup"
    #             <your>_cleanup_in_progress = False
    #             ->END
    #         <your>_destruction_source = "genuine_destruction"
    #
    # The flag is read and cleared HERE, in the destroy handler - never by the
    # code that called delete_object(). Clearing it at the call site is the bug
    # that was found and fixed live on 2026-08-08: the destroy hook had not run
    # yet, so the guard was already down by the time it did, and two GM cleanups
    # were both misreported as genuine kills.
    script.write_khovan_startup_trace("[KHOVAN LIB CLEANUP] deferred-destroy note label is documentation only")
    ->END
